# The fan's thermal zone runs step_wise, not the kernel default.
#
# The kernel's default governor here is power_allocator, which steers only a
# zone's last passive trip through cooling devices that have a power model. The
# fan has none, so under it the fan would sit wherever pwm-fan left it -- full
# duty, set at probe. step_wise walks the fan through the zone's active trips.
#
# Keyed on the zone's type, which is its device-tree node name ("fan-thermal",
# rk3566-microduck-beta.dts), never on thermal_zoneN: the number follows
# registration order. On a board with no such zone this matches nothing.
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="thermal", KERNEL=="thermal_zone*", ATTR{type}=="fan-thermal", ATTR{policy}="step_wise"
